## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates understanding of edge cryptography implementation, privacy-preserving design, and business impact analysis in payment systems—skills critical for roles at Cloudflare, Square, and similar fintech companies.

## Key Concepts
- On-device cryptographic verification using Ed25519 and platform crypto APIs
- Key management lifecycle and rotation strategies
- Mobile device constraints: latency, CPU, memory, and energy budgets
- Local telemetry architecture and storage growth patterns
- Regulatory compliance frameworks for payment verification
- Financial modeling with go/no-go criteria and break-even analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: verify an Ed25519 signature on-device
async function verifyReceipt(receipt, publicKey) {
  // receipt: { data: ArrayBuffer, signature: ArrayBuffer }
  const isValid = await crypto.subtle.verify(
    'Ed25519',
    publicKey,
    receipt.signature,
    receipt.data
  );
  return isValid;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates practical understanding of edge caching systems, cost modeling, and operational considerations for beginner-friendly distributed systems design.

## Key Concepts

- Edge caching strategies and TTL-based invalidation
- Delta synchronization for bandwidth optimization
- Energy-aware system design for battery-powered devices
- Phased rollout planning with cohort analysis
- Offline-first architecture and fallback behavior
- Privacy, compliance, and regulatory considerations

## Code Example

```javascript
function needsRefresh(lastRefresh, ttlHours) {
  const now = Date.now();
  const ttlMs = ttlHours * 60 * 60 * 1000;
  return (now - lastRefresh) >= ttlMs;
}

function getRefreshStrategy(device) {
  const batteryLevel = device.battery ?? 100;
  const isCharging = device.isCharging ?? false;

  if (batteryLevel < 20 && !isCharging) {
    return 'defer';
  } else if (batteryLevel < 50) {
    return 'adaptive';
  }
  return 'standard';
}
```

